<!-- SEPA-style pacs.004 return, namespace PREFIXED (urn2:) throughout.

     Three things this locks:
     1. the transaction subtree is prefixed, so recording it verbatim would
        produce a synthetic root that never closes (the same defect real
        prefixed pacs.008 messages exposed);
     2. the original parties are stated in <OrgnlTxRef>, which keeps the
        ORIGINAL sides — unlike <RtrChain> — so no crossing applies here;
     3. the settlement date sits once on <GrpHdr>, not on the transaction: SEPA
        does it that way, and a reader that only looks at the transaction
        returns NULL for every settlement date in the file.
     Shape from the OpenBankProject SEPA adapter's SEPA_SCT_IN pacs.004.001.02. -->
